  "claims": [
    "An ordinary inference model interprets each claim using only its declared finite condition support. It does not reconstruct the syntactic Cell or call a coherence generator.",
    "Ordinary closed derivations and geometric Cells admit rule-tree preserving translations in both directions within the same local-rule library. Applying the same deterministic shared compiler to each translated input yields equal output.",
    "An independent ordinary MAC-chain derivation has exactly 5*stage+2 tree nodes and condition support Finset.range(stage+1), for all stages.",
    "The geometric interpretation of the independent derivation exports exactly the same rule tree and checked compilation output. This specialization is a control, not an independent third proof-search algorithm.",
    "Finite-support ordinary repair uses cached conditions outside the change set and new proofs on its intersection, without geometric reconstruction."
  ],
